Track 3: Power Cut, Maracas Continue
Story & Context: The EP closer reenacts an actual rehearsal when the pavilion lost electricity during a storm. Mateo’s kick, sub and delay vanished instantly, but Damián continued the maraca cycle and Lucía refused to stop the harp pattern. Inés joined with dry muted cuatro until the three acoustic players had rebuilt the entire groove without electronics.

The studio version stages the same event deliberately. For the first half, dub-techno chords and sub pulses are prominent. On the sixth return of the main pattern, every powered device cuts to silence. Room microphones remain active on battery recorders, capturing foot taps, string buzz, maraca shells and the wooden floor. The ensemble continues for thirty-two bars acoustically.

When power returns, Mateo does not restore the full mix. He brings back only one low chord stab and a short tape-echo tail, letting the acoustic pulse remain dominant. The track ends with Damián counting twelve under his breath after the final harp note.

